[Music]  it's one of the most iconic hairstyles  of all time  bangs also known as fringe but we'll get  to that later  bangs have been immortalized by  countless movie stars and cultural icons  so where did bangs come from how does  one cut them and what does having bangs  say about the women bold enough to wear  them this is how bangs took over the  world  bangs date all the way back to the  eighth century people often credit the  Egyptian queen Cleopatra for bringing  them into style but that's just a myth  historians say the credit should go to  this guy his name was Surya  an Iraqi Renaissance man known to have  started the trend which as this painting  shows was also adopted by his female  fans over the next thousand years  bangs became an institution evident in  countless paintings of European women in  the 18th and 19th centuries with the  dawn of motion pictures silent film  stars like Louise Brooks made bangs and  iconic style of the roaring 20s  then came the era of the pin-up girl  pioneered by the notorious Bettie Page  Europe moved back into the spotlight in  the swinging 60s with iconic looks by  model Peggy Moffitt and singer Jane  Birkin only in Europe they don't call  them bangs they call it fringe which is  what the style is known as pretty much  everywhere except the u.s. so French  continued to evolve and sometimes the  results were mixed  but the look has endured and some of the  most iconic women in the world have made  sure that bangs or fringe whatever you  want to call it is one of the most  sought after styles on the planet and  those brave enough to get them usually  come with inspiration I love Taylor so  stings Taylor Swift Taylor Swift I'm a  stone reese witherspoon Alexa Chung  natalia dyer Zooey Deschanel Zooey  Deschanel have some great bangs so how  does one actually get bangs well that  depends on the type of bangs are going  for theirs blunt wispy shaggy choppy  curly side-swept the options are endless  [Music]  we went to Prima hair in the Lower East  Side of Manhattan to see how it's done  for both straight and curly hair when  summer with straight hair comes in for a  fringe generally we'll want to blow dry  the whole all of the hair forward to  make sure that we don't have any  partings in there draw the hair to the  center go ahead and cut and then soften  that line in through there  when someone has curly hair because the  hair doesn't quite sit the same way I  like to go through and cut each curl  individually to make sure that it's a  following the line in through there but  also shows movement as the curls go but  you don't have to go to a salon to get  fabulous bangs lots of women prefer to  do it themselves  [Music]  carefully so why do women get bangs well  let's ask them  my beings are a hundred percent a part  of my identity I just kind of wanted  this whole new look for a new chapter  sometimes I just like to switch it up  kind of cliche but I actually went to  Paris and a lot of girls had them and  they just looked so good I like the way  that they frame my face I feel like I  like myself with them more I grow them  at once and I absolutely hated it and  never did it again it was the first time  my haircut really felt like me because  it wasn't like my mom picking my  hairstyle for the first couple of days  it might want to live like this after a  week or so that fringe will start to  settle into its new position and make  your life a whole lot easier  bangs may look effortless but  maintaining them is anything but things  are super high maintenance it's easy to  put them in your hair but once they're  there it's a commitment for sure I  straighten them everyday with a  straightener the day's just split up  between pulling out the comb and  brushing them back down when it's really  windy out and like the winds hitting you  in both directions and then it goes up  and then you're like no that's not how I  look I promise in fact they can be so  high-maintenance it makes some women  swear off fringe forever  I actually am trying to grow out my  veins right now the one reason why I  hated them was because it was just like  an extra step in the morning I had bangs  of the baby because in the 90s that's  just normal  can you see this look how cute I was I  don't know people usually ask me oh why  I love  you had bangs and I'm like you loved me  with bangs but you wouldn't love having  them yourself that's pretty much what it  is it's just too much work but there are  shortcuts like these clip-in bangs which  don't require the months it takes to  grow them back out  bangs have been around for centuries  representing some of the most iconic  style moments of all time they may be a  lot of work but one thing is pretty  certain they're never going out of style  [Music]  I don't know just my face was way too  round for them and then after a while  I'd wear them on the side like that like  you can't really see that but like they  wouldn't fully cover my head like and  another thing is when you're growing  them out like some of these pictures I  have this is a picture of me doing it  whoops

